'''The''' '''''Nu''-class attack/transport shuttle''', also known as the '''''Nu''-class attack shuttle''' or '''Republic attack shuttle''', was a model of [[shuttle]] used by the [[Republic Navy]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="CloneWarsFilm" /> In the aftermath of the war, the Nu-class shuttles were absorbed into the fledgling [[Imperial Navy]].<ref name="Reunion">{{TBB|Reunion}}</ref> It was the predecessor of the [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]].<ref name="SWE" /> One [[transport]] fell into the hands of the [[Free Ryloth Movement]], and was used during the [[Mission to Ryloth (Phoenix Squadron)|Mission to Ryloth]].<ref name="Homecoming" />

==Characteristics==
Designed with fold-down wings, it was similar in design to later shuttles like the [[Theta-class T-2c shuttle|''Theta''-class]], [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class]], and [[Sentinel-class landing craft|''Sentinel''-class]]. Its boarding hatch was at the very front of the shuttle, unlike later variants, which had the cockpit jutting over the hatch. The [[pilot]]s' chairs lowered into the boarding area for them to enter and exit the [[cockpit]]. It also had a [[magnetic clamp]] on its ventral side capable of attaching to smaller payloads such as [[escape pod]]s.<ref name="Storm over Ryloth">{{TCW|Storm Over Ryloth}}</ref> The [[Rho-class transport shuttle|''Rho''-class transport shuttle]]<ref name="Rho DB">{{Databank|rho-class-transport-shuttle|Rho-class transport shuttle}}</ref> was visually very similar in appearance to the ''Nu''-class, but had an elongated hull, dorsal fin and the capability to attach cargo pods to its underside.<ref name="PONR">{{TCW|Point of No Return (The Clone Wars)}}</ref>

[[File:Clones-stand-for-Tarkin.png|thumb|left|300px|A ''Nu''-class shuttle in Imperial grey]]
It was primarily used by the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] for missions which required them to operate far away from bases and capital ships. Unlike the Republic's [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry|LAAT/i gunship]], the ''Nu''-class was also equipped with seats for the passengers due to much longer travel times.<ref name="The Gungan General">{{TCW|The Gungan General}}</ref>

Transports used by the [[Republic Navy]] during the [[Clone Wars]] had [[Color|red]] and yellow markings.<ref name="CloneWarsFilm" /> In the aftermath of the Clone Wars, ''Nu''-class shuttles were painted in a uniform, grey coloring as the Galactic Republic transitioned into the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Aftermath">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref>

{{Ship-stub}}

== History ==

=== Early use ===
{{Ship-stub}}
=== Clone Wars ===
A shuttle was eventually taken by the rouge Sith Lord [[Maul]] from the ''[[Tribunal]]'' [[Venator-class Star Destroyer]]<ref name="Victory and Death">{{TCW|Victory and Death}}</ref>

=== Imperial Era ===
Following the end of the war, Nu-class attack/transport shuttles became part of the Imperial Navy and were colored the typical grey of the [[Imperial Military]].<ref name="Kanan 4">[[Kanan 4|''Kanan'' 4]]</ref> 

One was used by Admiral Tarkin to visit Tipoca City on Kamino during his discussion with Prime Minister Lama Su in the Empire switching over to conscripted soldiers as a more cost effective alternative to the clones.<ref name="Aftermath episode">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref> Another was used by [[Crosshair]] and the [[Elite Squad]], consisting of [[ES-01]], [[ES-02]], [[ES-03]], and [[ES-04]] as part of the clandestine [[Project War-Mantle]] headed by [[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart]] during their [[Mission to Onderon (Elite Squad)|mission]] to [[Onderon]] to succeed where [[Clone Force 99]] failed in eliminating [[Saw Gerrera]]'s proto [[Partisans]]. The mission was a success even when losing ES-01, who protested the orders of shooting innocent civilians, though Gerrera had already left the world to gain new allies for the Partisans prior the squad arriving.<ref name="Replacements">{{TBB|Replacements}}</ref> 3 Nu-class attack/transport shuttles were later used by Crosshair and his Elite Squad in a [[Mission on Bracca|mission]] to [[Bracca]] to eliminate the former's old squad after [[Scrapper|scrappers]] identified them, one of which was ordered by Crosshair to find the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|''Marauder'']] while the other two converged on the abandoned [[Unidentified Venator-class Star Destroyer (Clone Force 99)|Venator]]<ref name="Reunion">{{TBB|Reunion}}</ref>

